Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:02.389 align:start position:0%
 
and we're joined now on the programme by  the deputy leader of the labour party  angela raynor ms reiner very good  morning to you  morning  so tell us what do you make of the  explanation such as it is  about the resignation of allegra  stratton about the parties that seem to  be taking across whitehall there is an  investigation now underway is that  enough  well it doesn't wash with me or the  general public i don't think i wrote to  the cabinet secretary last week asking  for an investigation into the one party  that we knew about at the time and the  prime minister at the time was saying  nothing to see here nothing happened i  find it incredulous that the prime  minister is saying that he didn't know  anything about a party at number 10 he's  now an alleged gathering party event  within his own flat they've had him also  at the conservative headquarters i mean  it's just fragrantly disregard and  laughing at the public and taking them  for fools around the rules but what i  will say and what i think is really  important and this is why labour have  been supporting the efforts and want us  to go further in terms of providing sick  pay and ventilation in our schools we we  have to follow these guidance because  it's not what boris johnson says it's  about keeping us all safe because the  chief medical officer and the science  says that we need to take this action to  protect ourselves and to protect the nhs  who have been you know diligently  looking after us throughout this  pandemic and we know winter is a  difficult time for our nhs so we do have  to act responsibly and by the way the  vast majority of the public understand  this and have been doing it and that's  why they're really angry at the prime  minister  allowing  this to happen under his watch within  the heart of downing street is an  absolute disgrace and he's got trap  records you know this is a guy in every  elected position that he's ever held  he's broke the rules so it's his time's  up you can't do it as prime minister  especially not when lives are at risk  sure but but from what you've just said  and the support given by the shadow  health secretary to the move to plan b  yesterday you don't feel unlike some  conservative mps in fact that the rather  abrupt move to plan b was in any way  linked to that release of the video  showing  most likely that a party did take place  in number 10 and the rules were broken  well you know what's really important is  that you know we had a meeting and  kirsten spoke to the chief medical  officer and you know had a briefing from  those in the position of knowledge who  said that we need to take these measures  so the labour party are clear that we're  following the medical and the science  and expert advice on this and we  hope that people will do that boris  johnson has completely undermined those  efforts and we you know it's incredibly  disappointing i am calling on the  government today to provide sick pay for  people this is a massive big problem  when it comes to people being able to do  the right thing and self-isolate they  need sick pace so that that can happen  and that will help control the virus and  we need to make sure that we have proper  ventilation in schools it's cold this  time of year many schools have still not  got adequate ventilation we know this  would help and we know the infection  spreads in school so we're calling on  the government to really step up their  efforts to make sure that people have  got access to the booster jobs access to  vaccines but also they fix six pet sick  pay and that they start out the  situation with ventilation in our  schools  we also know that you know despite the  prime minister's entreaty to us all to  continue with our christmas parties the  measures announced yesterday uh well and  indeed just the current vibe around  government not exactly lending itself to  confidence within the hospitality sector  it feels as if they will start losing  money now if if not in the in the  immediate future  is the labour party's position that  there should once again be some form of  financial assistance for businesses who  are affected by the increased  restrictions  well what was important is that if you  look at what the welsh look at labour  government did they brought in the  vaccine passports and testing negative  testing some time ago which gave  business the opportunity to respond to  this the government have to support  business to ensure that they can take  adequate measures so that that people  can be safe and can go out to events in  a safe manner we're also asking people  to if you are going to a christmas party  or you are going to an event where  there'll be more people and it's  particularly indoors is that you do take  a test beforehand so that you know  you're not carrying the virus we can all  act responsibly so that we can continue  to  live as normal life as possible and we  think the government should do that but  you know doing it last minute is a  problem for businesses they they find it  very difficult especially this being  their busiest time of year to respond to  last minute changes and we feel like the  government should have been planning for  this some time ago rather than bringing  it last minute for businesses and them  trying to adapt so the government really  do need to support business to to adapt  to the changes that we need to make  just a couple of questions if we can  away from covert for a second there was  there was an article um recently in the  manchester evening news saying that that  your son has asked you to step down from  from frontline politics because of the  the number of threats you've received  your mother believes that there are  people trying to trying to kill you what  what is the the extent of the of the  threats that are being made against you  at the moment if you don't mind me  asking  well and and  and unfortunately this isn't just a  singular issue for me it's cross-party  actually and it's a lot of and it's  predominantly female members of  parliament from all of the different  political parties seem to get a  significant amount of threats some of  them are death threats i've had death  threats against me threats against my  children told me that it wasn't hard to  find where i live and that i should do  them a favor and just kill myself rather  than them having to hunt me down like my  friend which was obviously the uh joe  cox who was who was a friend of mine who  was murdered in battle and spent so it's  pretty nasty stuff but you know the  police have been great manchester police  in particular have been incredibly  supportive and have been supporting me  and my family through it but my 12 and  13 year old have had to learn how to use  panic buttons and have escape routes  from our house and their lives have  changed because of it but the most  important thing to me is that these  people will not stop me doing my job and  representing  the constituents that i have the honor  to represent and that is what most mps  feel at the moment and it is a minority  who feel that you know they can try and  silence us as mps but that won't happen  because that is our democracy and we  have had a huge amount of support from  the police forces to make sure that we  can continue with our role but it is  upsetting and distressing for our family  and our staff who have to read through  countless levels of abuse that's level  that us and also unfortunately death  threats which like i say is not unique  to me  it has happened in a significant amount  of the time to many mps from all  different political parties  just just just before we let you go i  want to ask about the state of relations  between you and you and kirsten you were  sitting side by side at prime minister's  questions yesterday are you back to  being best buddies i'm just wondering  whether the suspension of your head of  communications jack mckenna might have  acted to stymie that perhaps  well me and kyr have had an incredibly  constructive relationship ever since we  became leader and deputy leader of the  labour party and we continue to do that  because we're both absolutely  clear that we need a labour government  and we work constructively together we  are different people of course we are  but you know kerry is the leader of the  labour party and i'm his deputy and we  work together you know very well  i won't comment on issues to do with  staff because i don't think that's  that's fair to do that there is  processes that go through and you know  those processes will continue and i  don't think it's it's right that that's  you know played out in the media as i  said before my staff have been through a  hell of a lot um coping with you know  helping constituents and supporting me  and doing my role so i i won't comment  on individual staff members but what i  will say is me and kyra are very clear  and have never departed from that and  continue to be joined together in making  sure that we show that we are a labor  government in waiting and that we will  change working people's lives and change  people's lives for the better once we're  in government  angela rainer good to have you on the  program this morning thanks for being  with us  thank you

